# Every change to a Terraform repository needs a platform owner's approval:
# GitHub asks the code owners to review every pull request, and the branch
# rules for every tier require their approval. Application repositories are
# owned by the lead developers instead (repository-template).
#
# Keep one owning team. When a line lists several owners, an approval from any
# one of them counts, so a second team here could stand in for the first.
# The team needs write access to count: platform.auto.tfvars gives it
# team_access on every repository created from this template.
*       @{{ORGANIZATION}}/{{PLATFORM_OWNERS_TEAM}}
